{#
  Page FAQ — layout-level "Common questions" block, single-sourced from the
  `faq` front-matter array of q/a pairs. Rendered once from base.njk (body),
  after {{ content }} and BEFORE the related strip. Renders nothing when `faq`
  is absent (exactly like the related strip and feedback widget — the third
  member of that layout-level family). See STYLE_GUIDE §6.40.

    faq:
      - q: "How much bitcoin do I need to retire?"
        a: "There is no single number …"     # may contain a safe inline <a>

  The matching FAQPage JSON-LD is emitted from components/faq-schema.njk in
  <head> from the SAME array — edit the front matter only; both follow, so the
  schema can never drift from the visible text (a Google-policy correctness
  issue, not just tidiness).

  NOT collapsible: every answer is in the DOM on load (Google policy forbids
  schema describing click-injected content; also the accessible default). A
  plain h2 + h3/p stack, per the rules doc.

  Answer markup: `| safe` so a curated inline link renders; the JSON-LD copy
  strips tags to plain text so the two still match as strings.
#}
{%- if faq and faq.length > 0 -%}
<section class="page-faq" id="faq" aria-label="Common questions">
  <h2 class="page-faq-title">Common questions</h2>
{%- for item in faq %}
  <h3 class="faq-q">{{ item.q | safe }}</h3>
  <p class="faq-a">{{ item.a | safe }}</p>
{%- endfor %}
</section>
{%- endif -%}
